 "id": "eval-design-spaghetti-shelf",
 "backend": "cad",
 "brief": {
  "goal": "a tall open shelving unit after the Spaghetti Shelf System by Frederik Fialin, 1200mm wide, 370mm deep and 2500mm tall: four vertical 16mm stainless steel rods, 800mm apart along the width and 300mm apart front to back, each standing on a small levelling foot; six 1200x370x18mm okoume plywood shelves evenly spaced from 300mm up to 2300mm, overhanging the rods by 200mm at each end. Each shelf rests on two stainless cross brackets, a flat bar running front to back under the shelf with a clamp block at each end gripping a rod by a hand-tightened thumb screw, so the levels can be moved and the unit taken apart without tools.",
  "design": "Quiet minimalist furniture after Fialin's Spaghetti shelf: slender brushed-stainless lines against warm, flat plywood. Steel parts get small crisp chamfers and no decoration. Plywood edges get a light eased round so the laminations read cleanly. Everything should look deliberately thin and light, never chunky.",
  "refs": []
 },
